From 9e7d80c1c62b7e0e4f0292b6db317dad306aaff2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 14:44:13 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Shrink the KISS PRNG lag table from 16 MiB to 32 KiB

rand.c keeps a static table of 0x200000 uint64_t (16 MiB), and
randk_seed() writes every entry, so all of it becomes resident. The file
is linked into the client and again into game.so, so a running game
holds 32 MiB for random numbers. On a machine with 217 MB of RAM
(PS3, ppc64) that is 15% of memory.

Use 0x1000 entries (32 KiB). The generator is seeded the same way, so
only the length of the lag table changes. Nothing in the game needs
the very long period of the large table: randk() serves monster
decisions, damage rolls, challenge numbers and similar.

Measured on a PS3 (Cell PPE, 217 MB RAM, swap on a VRAM block device
and zram) with q2demo1 on Yamagi Quake II 8.70: resident set of the
process 125 -> 56 MB, swap in use 80 -> 9 MB, time spent in frames
over 100 ms during gameplay 22.6 s -> 0.05 s, steady 65.7 -> 68.7 fps.
---
 src/common/shared/rand.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/common/shared/rand.c b/src/common/shared/rand.c
index 869bca1..cec194d 100644
--- a/src/common/shared/rand.c
+++ b/src/common/shared/rand.c
@@ -15,7 +15,13 @@
 
 #include <stdint.h>
 
-#define QSIZE 0x200000
+/*
+ * Size of the lag table, a power of two. It used to be 0x200000
+ * entries (16 MiB), written completely by randk_seed() and linked
+ * into the client and into every game module. 4096 entries (32 KiB)
+ * is plenty for what the game draws.
+ */
+#define QSIZE 0x1000
 #define CNG (cng = 6906969069ULL * cng + 13579)
 #define XS (xs ^= (xs << 13), xs ^= (xs >> 17), xs ^= (xs << 43))
 #define KISS (B64MWC() + CNG + XS)
